From: Kefu Chai <k.chai@proxmox.com>
Subject: [PATCH librados2-perl v2] do not shut down the handle twice if a
 signal arrives at exit
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:54:09 +0800

When a task runs in the foreground from the command line,
fork_worker() sends SIGTERM to the worker's process group once the
worker exits. The worker's pverados child is in that group, and it is
often already shutting down the handle after seeing EOF. The handler
then calls rados_shutdown() on the freed handle, and the child
segfaults:

  pverados[...]: segfault at 3bc0 ... in libc.so.6[95ba0,...]

This affects commands like 'pveceph pool create' or 'pvesh create
/nodes/<node>/ceph/pool', whose worker opens a RADOS connection. It is
a race, but on a test cluster with Ceph 21.1.2, 'pveceph pool create'
crashed this way in all four runs. Tasks started from the GUI or the
API run in the background. Their process group is not signalled at
the end, and they did not crash.

The crash is a regression from commit 8cab00f ("reset inherited signal
handlers in child worker"), first released in librados2-perl 1.4.1 in
August 2023. Before that, the child kept the worker's handler, which
dies instead of shutting down the handle again. The new handlers also
outlived the eval, since the 'local' only covered $SIG{HUP}.

So ignore the signals before shutting down, and install the handlers
first thing in the child.

Tested-by: Maximiliano Sandoval <m.sandoval@proxmox.com>
Signed-off-by: Kefu Chai <k.chai@proxmox.com>
---
Changes since v1 [1]:
- say in the commit message which setups are affected and since when,
  as Maximiliano asked. The code is unchanged.

[1] https://lore.proxmox.com/pve-devel/20261020141223.2814127-1-k.chai@proxmox.com/

 PVE/RADOS.pm | 19 ++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/PVE/RADOS.pm b/PVE/RADOS.pm
index 5a79235..deb4912 100644
--- a/PVE/RADOS.pm
+++ b/PVE/RADOS.pm
@@ -200,6 +200,17 @@ sub new {
     } else { # child
 	$0 = 'pverados';
 
+	my @signals = qw(HUP INT QUIT TERM);
+
+	# ignore signals from here on, the handler must not shut down a freed handle
+	my $shutdown = sub {
+	    @SIG{@signals} = ('IGNORE') x @signals;
+	    pve_rados_shutdown($self->{conn}) if $self->{conn};
+	};
+
+	# override signal handlers inherited from the parent
+	@SIG{@signals} = (sub { $shutdown->(); POSIX::_exit(1); }) x @signals;
+
 	eval {
 	    PVE::INotify::inotify_close();
 
@@ -207,12 +218,6 @@ sub new {
 		&$atfork();
 	    }
 
-	    # override signal handlers inherited from the parent
-	    local $SIG{HUP} = $SIG{INT} = $SIG{QUIT} = $SIG{TERM} = sub {
-		pve_rados_shutdown($self->{conn}) if $self->{conn};
-		POSIX::_exit(1);
-	    };
-
 	    # fixme: timeout?
 
 	    close $child;
@@ -222,7 +227,7 @@ sub new {
 	my $err = $@;
 	warn $err if $err;
 
-	pve_rados_shutdown($self->{conn}) if $self->{conn};
+	$shutdown->();
 	POSIX::_exit($err ? 1 : 0);
     }
 
